## What was wrong

The task died partway through step 3 of its own protocol. The round-75 prediction was sealed and committed (3a21b380), but the grade never landed — exactly the failure mode tests/blind_round_grades.rs was built to catch, so the gate correctly failed the run rather than letting a half-written round ship.

## What I found before fixing

The mutation run had actually happened — and was **still executing** when I picked it up. `end_time: null`, lock file held, and the summary counters disagreeing with the live per-function tally (1 missed vs 2). My read of the outcomes file grew from 30 → 32 → 34 entries across successive reads. I waited for the process to exit and re-derived every number from the raw outcomes array rather than the summary. Had I graded on first read I'd have published 3.3% from an unfinished run.

## The reading

34 mutants: 31 caught, 3 missed, 0 unviable — 8.8% survival, identical on both denominators since nothing was unviable. All 3 survivors are comparison swaps on > 0 guards in the renderer; both parsing functions are clean at 0/19.

I also confirmed the mandated trap check: this module has zero `#[test]` functions (its 13 tests live in a sibling file), so the rounds-73/74 habit of filtering on the module name would have selected 0 tests and reported a vacuous 100% survival. Pre-flight returned 13 passed, so the filter was right.

## Grades: 1 hit / 1 partial / 2 miss

I graded against the sealed text, and the two misses are the substance: h1 and h2 deliberately bet against round 74's finding, and both lost — h1 named zero survivors on precisely the guards that turned out to be the only unpinned thing in the file. h3 is the one hit, and I checked it was non-vacuous (4 counter mutants genuinely generated, all caught) rather than accepting a "zero survivors" claim where nothing was tested.

The n=3 answer: the instrument-vs-product gap inverted. 8.8% against 32.0% (product) and 41.5% (instrument). The two-day pattern is dead — which was the outcome this target was chosen to make possible.

